rpn: unknown option '-z'
usage: rpn [-h] [-v] [-q] [-s N] [-l file] [-x file] [file ...]
  -h       show this text
  -v       show the version
  -q       do not echo the top of the stack after each line
  -s N     maximum stack depth (default 100)
  -l file  load a file silently and carry on
  -x file  execute a file, then stop (stdin is not read)
Options are case-insensitive.
Commands exit (status = top of stack, 0..255) and quit end the run.
Reads standard input when no file (or "-") is given.
